    {
      "source": "hn",
      "title": "Show HN: Drive around my village in 3D",
      "url": "https://cherwellvalleymotorclub.app",
      "author": "johnwards",
      "external_id": "50574412",
      "summary": null,
      "why_read": null,
      "authors": [],
      "category": null,
      "published": "2026-11-20T13:32:42Z",
      "score": 66,
      "comments": 50,
      "hn_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50574412",
      "snippet": "So this started out just over a week ago, could I drive around my village in my old car on the web, and its expanded into a massive map, with races, events, different cars and multiplayer.<p>I&#x27;m a web&#x2F;app guy, backend guy, and yes I build it with Claude.<p>I know I shouldn&#x27;t be astounded by what these Ai agents can do as of today, but here I am still amazed.<p>I&#x27;ve even got support from a Sim racing guy and built a web driver so he gets full force feedback for his rig, and it works.<p>Anyway, just a bit of fun!<p>Uses LIDAR data from the UK Gov + OpenStreetMap data to build the world. Technically, I could do the whole of England&#x2F;Wales...but the data storage would be huge!",
      "links": []
    },
